"""Install the "Cursor Concept W11 Tail HDPi" mouse pointers for this user.

    lapin-ux-cursors [--dark] [--variant NAME] [--from DIR]
    lapin-ux-cursors --system        (back to the system's own pointer)
    lapin-ux-cursors --theme NAME    (any installed pointer theme, by folder name)

Cursor design by JepriCreations — https://www.deviantart.com/jepricreations
and https://jepricreations.com. Its author doesn't allow the cursor files to
be redistributed, so Lapin UX doesn't ship them: this downloads the pack on
your computer (from the copy at github.com/SullensCR/Windows-11-Hdpi-Tail-
Cursor-Concept-by-jepriCreations, or a folder you give with --from),
converts the Windows .cur/.ani files to an X cursor theme for your own use,
installs it under ~/.local/share/icons and makes it your pointer.

The pack keeps its author's name; it is not renamed or claimed as Lapin UX's.
Needs Python's Pillow (python-pillow).
"""
